-- exact angular momentum (Avik, 2026-11-18: "that means there is plenty of fucking low hanging fruit
-- visible by novel mathematical clarity ... go savage mode"). The amplitudes that couple spins — two
-- electrons into a bond pair, the shells of an atom, the edges of a spin network — are Clebsch–Gordan
-- coefficients, and Racah's formula gives each as a sign times the square root of a rational: a finite
-- sum of reciprocals of factorials under a square root of a ratio of factorials. So every one is exact,
-- with no real number formed: the sign and the rational square are computed, and a probability (the
-- square) is a rational. Spins are carried doubled (tj = 2j) and projections as j + m, so every
-- argument is a natural number.

